Supported Query Patterns for Dependencies:

==========================================
1. ARROW SYNTAX (EXPLICIT INSTRUCTIONS) - NEW!
==========================================

Format: Action -> Instruction1 -> Instruction2

Example 1: Extract and Use
Create a new pet -> Retrieve the pet_id from the response
Update pet information -> Use the pet_id from previous response
Delete a pet -> Use the pet_id from previous response

Example 2: Multiple Fields
Create a user -> Extract the user_id and email from response
Create order -> Use the user_id from previous response
Update order -> Use the same user_id

Example 3: Specific Field Names
Create a new pet -> Save the id from response
Update pet -> Pass the id from previous response to this request
Delete pet -> Send the id from previous response

Supported Keywords:
- Extract: retrieve, extract, save, get
- Use: use, pass, send, with


==========================================
2. EXPLICIT STEP REFERENCE
==========================================

Create a new pet in the pet store
Update pet from step 1
Delete pet from step 1


==========================================
3. "PREVIOUS" KEYWORD
==========================================

Create a new pet in the pet store
Update the previous pet
Delete the previous pet


==========================================
4. "CREATED/UPDATED/SAME" KEYWORDS
==========================================

Create a new pet in the pet store
Update the created pet
Delete the same pet


==========================================
5. IMPLICIT (AUTOMATIC)
==========================================

Create a new pet in the pet store
Update the pet information
Delete a pet

(Automatically detects {petId} path parameter and uses extracted ID)


==========================================
EXAMPLES BY USE CASE
==========================================

Use Case 1: Simple CRUD with Arrow Syntax
-----------------------------------------

Create a new pet -> Retrieve the pet_id from the response
Update the pet -> Use the pet_id from previous response
Delete the pet -> Use the pet_id from previous response


Use Case 2: User and Order Workflow
-----------------------------------

Create a new user -> Extract the user_id from response
Create an order -> Use the user_id from previous response
Get order details -> Use the order_id from step 2
Cancel the order -> Use the order_id from previous response


Use Case 3: Implicit Dependencies
---------------------------------

Create a new pet
Update the pet information
Delete a pet

(Works automatically without explicit instructions)


==========================================
TIPS
==========================================

1. Use arrow syntax (->) for explicit control over field extraction
2. Field names are case-insensitive and underscore-flexible (pet_id = petId)
3. Multiple queries separated by semicolon (;)
4. Extraction happens automatically for POST/PUT if subsequent steps need IDs
5. You can mix patterns (some with arrows, some without)


